---
import MainLayout from "../../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

// We use the high-end hero image generated
import blogHero from "../../../assets/fin-aplicaciones-pesadas.png";
---

<MainLayout title="The end of heavy applications: Why the future is (and will be) 100% Web | Otterock Blog">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-20 px-6">
    <header class="mb-12 text-center">
      <a
        href="/en/blog"
        class="inline-block mb-8 text-otter-deep font-bold hover:text-otter-accent transition-colors"
      >
        ← Back to Blog
      </a>

      <span
        class="text-slate-600 font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-xs mb-4 block"
      >
        Technology • 5 min read
      </span>

      <h1
        class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-black text-otter-deep mb-6 leading-tight font-display"
      >
        The end of heavy applications: Why the future is (and will be) 100% Web
      </h1>

      <p class="text-xl text-slate-700 italic font-body mb-8">
        "We are entering an era where it will no longer be profitable (or efficient) to have giant applications installed on our computers. The future is web."
      </p>

      <div
        class="rounded-3xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl mb-12 aspect-video bg-otter-deep"
      >
        <Image
          src={blogHero}
          alt="The future of web applications"
          width={800}
          quality="mid"
          format="webp"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-90"
        />
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-lg text-slate-700 leading-relaxed font-body">
      <p
        class="first-letter:text-5xl first-letter:font-bold first-letter:text-otter-deep first-letter:mr-2 first-letter:float-left"
      >
        A few days ago, watching an analysis by Nate Gentile about Apple's new hardware, I came across a reflection that fascinated me and confirms what we have been promoting at Otterock: hardware is changing, and with it, the way we consume software.
      </p>

      <p>
        The conclusion is clear: we are entering an era where it will no longer be profitable (or efficient) to have giant applications installed on our devices. The future is web, and here we explain why your business should be there right now.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-otter-deep/10 my-12" />

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-6 font-display">
          1. The RAM Crisis and the Rise of AI
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          As Nate pointed out, current hardware — even the most powerful processors derived from the iPhone 16 Pro Max — has a new enemy: local Artificial Intelligence. Language models and AI tools consume RAM at levels never seen before.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-6">
          This creates a bottleneck. If the computers of the near future are going to use a large part of their power just to keep AI alive, there will be no room for heavy applications running natively.
        </p>

        <div
          class="bg-otter-sand/50 p-6 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-otter-deep my-8"
        >
          <p class="text-slate-800 font-bold mb-2">The solution?</p>
          <p class="text-slate-700">
            Web applications that run on powerful servers and are delivered lightly to the user. Your hardware doesn't suffer; the cloud does the dirty work.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-6 font-display mt-12">
          2. The "Pros of Pros" of Betting on the Web
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Building a website or web application today is not just about "having a presence"; it's about preparing for the standard of the next decade. Here are the definitive benefits:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-3">A. Total Universality (Zero Friction)</h3>
            <p>
              A native application forces you to download, install, and update. A Web App is one click away. It doesn't matter if your customer has the latest Mac or a mid-range phone; if they have a browser, they have your business. It's the fluidity of the otter at its peak.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-3">B. Centralized Maintenance</h3>
            <p>
              Forget about old versions. When we update a web application at Otterock, the change is instantaneous for all users. There are no patches, no errors due to lack of disk space on the customer's side. The "firmness of the rock" is on the server.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-3">C. Smart Infrastructure Costs</h3>
            <p>
              Developing for iOS, Android, Windows, and Mac separately is astronomically expensive. A well-built web application (using technologies like Astro and Tailwind CSS v4) works everywhere with a single development. Less expense, more reach.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-6 font-display mt-12">
          3. The Browser is the New Operating System
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          We're already seeing it. Professional design tools, video editors, and complex management systems already live in the browser. The web is no longer just for "reading information"; it's for executing processes.
        </p>

        <p class="mb-6">
          At Otterock, we specialize in this paradigm shift. We don't make sites that "look good," we build tools that:
        </p>

        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4 text-slate-700 italic mb-8">
          <li>Don't consume your customer's resources.</li>
          <li>Are ultra-fast thanks to Edge Computing.</li>
          <li>Scale to infinity with databases like Supabase.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-otter-deep/10 my-12" />

      <section class="text-center">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-6 font-display">
          Conclusion: Don't Stay Behind
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-8">
          If tech giants are designing processors thinking that heavy software will live in the cloud, why are you still offering slow or limited solutions to your customers?
        </p>
        <p class="mb-8">
          Betting on a web architecture today is guaranteeing that your business is accessible, fast, and modern, no matter how much RAM tomorrow's AI consumes.
        </p>
        <p class="text-2xl font-black text-otter-deep mb-12">
          At Otterock, we don't just write code; we design the future of your digital sovereignty.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section
        class="bg-otter-deep text-white p-8 md:p-12 rounded-3xl text-center relative overflow-hidden"
      >
        <div
          class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-white/10 rounded-full -mr-10 -mt-10 blur-2xl"
        >
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold font-display mb-4 relative z-10">
          Ready for the future of the web?
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-8 opacity-90 leading-relaxed relative z-10">
          Let's build together a tool that not only looks great but also works incredibly on any device.
        </p>

        <a
          href="/en/contacto"
          class="inline-block bg-white text-otter-deep px-8 py-4 rounded-full font-bold hover:bg-otter-accent hover:text-white transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 shadow-lg relative z-10"
        >
          I want to evolve my business
        </a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</MainLayout>
